  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This may be a little long sorry!\n\nMaybe instead of uploading the avatars to the VRChat servers, have them save on the client computer in a format that VRChat can read (much like a mods for a game) and then is opened up in VRChat when the user logs in (default avatar/last used) or the files are listed when a user goes to select an avatar, and then is opened up if the user changes to that avatar.\nNow for other people viewing the avatar, have the client computer upload the model to the server/world the user is connecting to, and have all users on server/world download it. And when a user leaves/changes to a different model, the model the user was using is removed from the server/world and is also removed from all the clients currently connected to the server/world (this also affects the user who left, with the exception of the avatar the user was using).\n\nNow this can also be a way to remove the polygon limit when uploading an avatar, and in the settings of the game, you can have an option to limit the size of models you are downloading to only download models under a certain polygon limit, and helps with the lag some users may have. But let this limit have a 'default' value, but also a custom value in case someone wants to use a model with a high poly limit, or the user believes their computer can handle a lot of polygons.\n\nThis option may also save VRChat themselves some money on servers if how the servers are being paid for is only by the storage and not by internet traffic.",
